# Premium README

A README that looks like a product page and reads like an engineering document.

Choose the procedure, read it in full, and follow it:

- Apply or rewrite: <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jeancarlosaps/premium-readme-template/main/prompts/apply-to-project.md>
- Audit: <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jeancarlosaps/premium-readme-template/main/prompts/audit-existing-readme.md>
- Illustrations only: <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jeancarlosaps/premium-readme-template/main/prompts/create-visual-assets.md>

If you cannot fetch URLs, ask the user to clone the template and add it to the workspace, then read the same paths locally.

Essentials, always:

- Documentation only. Never change application code, dependencies or CI without permission.
- Every claim traces to a file, a command you ran or an output you saw. No invented features, results, badges or roadmap.
- Original SVG assets in the project's own identity. Animated hero runs once, ≤ 4 s, respects `prefers-reduced-motion`, and has a generated `hero-still.svg`.
- Essential information lives in Markdown, not only in images. Every image has useful alt text.
- Work on a branch, validate, review the diff, open a pull request. Never commit to the default branch, never merge.
- Report what you could not verify.
